{"data": [{"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-25T20:44:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114458036320215115"], "id": "2114458036320215115", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 4221, "like_count": 20, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Wow great goal from Mbappé", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2114458036320215115"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-25T20:35:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114455817730875404"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/401casey/statu…", "end": 146, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/401casey/status/2114454727832318190", "start": 123, "url": "https://t.co/49qNjOYQZC"}]}, "id": "2114455817730875404", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 6792, "like_count": 61, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 16, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114454727832318190", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Like I said, all I eat anymore is meat and fermented veggies. Completely addicted to kimchi after just 5 days of this diet https://t.co/49qNjOYQZC", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2114455817730875404"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-25T20:06:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114448563547562271"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/nkulw/status/2…", "end": 124, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/nkulw/status/2114446236077994444", "start": 101, "url": "https://t.co/HMPrbhXwf9"}]}, "id": "2114448563547562271", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 11332, "like_count": 59, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 34, "retweet_count": 5}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114446236077994444", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I agree with all this. But what I’m curious about is: What is the worldview of the self-driving car? https://t.co/HMPrbhXwf9", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2114448563547562271"}, {"author_id": "917683048782503937", "created_at": "2026-10-25T19:48:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114443907886927994"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Pessimism has gripped Chinese stocks, with no end in sight for a deepening selloff as investors confront the realities of an economy that’s weak enough to erode corporate profits but not to trigger forceful new stimulus.", "display_url": "bloomberg.com/news/articles/…", "end": 242, "expanded_url": "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-10-25/sinking-profits-turn-china-s-3-5-trillion-stock-rout-into-trap?utm_source=website&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=twitter", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114188398491791360/3ozifQ4u?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114188398491791360/3ozifQ4u?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 219, "status": 200, "title": "Sinking Profits Turn China’s $3.5 Trillion Stock Rout Into Trap", "unwound_url": "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-10-25/sinking-profits-turn-china-s-3-5-trillion-stock-rout-into-trap?utm_source=website&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=twitter", "url": "https://t.co/cJjf5PYngi"}]}, "id": "2114443907886927994", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 4579, "like_count": 33, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "Bloomberg: “At the heart of investor gloom is an unsettling realization that a protracted consumption slump and the race-to-the-bottom mentality among businesses is taking a heavier toll on earnings across industries.”\nhttps://t.co/cJjf5PYngi", "url": "https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2114443907886927994"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-25T19:19:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114436780963270823"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 48, "id": "1707509996265558016", "start": 37, "username": "LSCCountry"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/holliemaea/sta…", "end": 131, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/holliemaea/status/2114433969454535124", "start": 108, "url": "https://t.co/OnE9zRVYd2"}]}, "id": "2114436780963270823", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 9327, "like_count": 21, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114433969454535124", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "That’s right. And you can come watch @LSCCountry play country music FREE this Wednesday @ Lucinda’s at 8:30 https://t.co/OnE9zRVYd2", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2114436780963270823"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-25T18:17:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114421049047564418"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "The Federal Communications Commission ​said on Thursday it ‌blocked two devices from the US market ​that contain ​foreign surveillance chips produced by ⁠a subsidiary ​of China's Huawei, the ​first time it has exercised authority under new ​rules.", "display_url": "reuters.com/world/us-block…", "end": 249, "expanded_url": "https://www.reuters.com/world/us-blocks-two-devices-with-chinese-made-surveillance-chips-2026-10-22/", "images": [{"height": 1005, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113338105059020800/_byQKB7n?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1920}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113338105059020800/_byQKB7n?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 226, "status": 200, "title": "US blocks two devices with Chinese-made surveillance chips", "unwound_url": "https://www.reuters.com/world/us-blocks-two-devices-with-chinese-made-surveillance-chips-2026-10-22/", "url": "https://t.co/Wq6AkCtoPM"}]}, "id": "2114421049047564418", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1288, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "\"The Federal Communications Commission said Thurs it ‌had blocked 2 devices from the US market that contain foreign surveillance chips produced by a Huawei subsidiary, the 1st time it had exercised authority under new ⁠rules\"\nhttps://t.co/Wq6AkCtoPM", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2114421049047564418"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-25T17:19:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114406391914152222"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/jstek52/status…", "end": 192, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/jstek52/status/2114044016660525133", "start": 169, "url": "https://t.co/KE7y7I01hZ"}]}, "id": "2114406391914152222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1445, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114044016660525133", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Great question and I think the answer is contingent\n\nIf you want to measure *demand growth* then use “core demand”\n\nBut it’s functioning poorly as a de-noised GDP proxy https://t.co/KE7y7I01hZ", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2114406391914152222"}, {"author_id": "423769635", "created_at": "2026-10-25T17:07:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114403563229393269"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 174, "id": "1153704552228630528", "start": 162, "username": "steve_donze"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/fv5rQ04h8j", "end": 198, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2114403563229393269/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114403497311449088", "start": 175, "url": "https://t.co/fv5rQ04h8j"}]}, "id": "2114403563229393269", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 12, "impression_count": 5751, "like_count": 44, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 15, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "Unlike the dot-com bubble, when global technology stocks surged far ahead of earnings, the current rally has been supported by stronger earnings growth.\n\nSource: @steve_donze https://t.co/fv5rQ04h8j", "url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2114403563229393269"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-25T16:51:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114399480720380